WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.913
- Sorry for having 43 tardies.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.404
(laughing)

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.737
(pop music)

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.570
- I have certain teachers that are cool,

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.360
and they'll be like, "Well,
do you need help with this?"

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.960
And they'll like, hold you after class

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.090
and help you out with stuff.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.633
Well others, they don't care.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.327
They're just, "Okay, I'm here to teach,

00:00:19.327 --> 00:00:20.530
"get paid, and leave."

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.060
- Something I hate about teachers

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.770
is that sometimes they
give too much homework.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:28.032
Or they expect a lot but they don't really

00:00:28.032 --> 00:00:30.203
give a good lesson.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.973
(pop music)

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.290
- On average, how much did
teachers spend out of pocket

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.453
in 2016 on supplies for
the classroom and students?

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.140
- I mean, like, in elementary school,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.833
you use like, crayons and markers.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.570
- In high school, it's basically
all given to you, I think.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:49.103
- 260. We usually bought the supplies, so.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:50.668
- I'd say like the middle, 480.

00:00:50.668 --> 00:00:51.668
- Yeah, 480.

00:00:52.392 --> 00:00:53.225
- D, 480.
- D.

00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:54.058
(bell dinging)

00:00:54.058 --> 00:00:54.891
- No way.
- No.

00:00:54.891 --> 00:00:56.640
- I thought that the school
gave them everything.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.390
- I have a specific
teacher who, she gets there

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.100
at 6:00 in the morning for
help sessions until 8:00,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.020
and then after school she
stays there until 6:00,

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.340
so it's like an extra
two hours she's there

00:01:07.384 --> 00:01:09.010
before and after school.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.110
She's not getting paid for it, either,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.180
but she's just there to
make sure us students

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.970
are succeeding in her class.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:17.320
As of 2014, over what percent
of public school teachers

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.163
in the US work second
jobs outside of school?

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.710
I know they're not paid a lot.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:22.623
- C?

00:01:22.813 --> 00:01:24.490
- Yeah.
- Yeah, so 30%.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.910
- So C, 30%.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:26.970
- I think 20%.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.723
- A, 20%.
- Yeah.

00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:30.300
(bell dinging)
- That's still a lot, though.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.820
- [Man] Would you guys become teachers?

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.673
- Yes.
- No.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.330
You? (laughing)

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.163
- Yeah.

00:01:35.163 --> 00:01:37.990
Almost what percentage of
teachers quit within five years

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.640
of starting their teaching career?

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.503
- My teachers from elementary school,

00:01:41.842 --> 00:01:42.920
they were like one and done, so --

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.350
- Oh really?
- ... they would do a year,

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.510
and then they would leave.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.070
- Maybe, C, 20%?

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.937
- Yeah. C, 20%.
- C, 20%.

00:01:49.361 --> 00:01:50.461
(bell dinging)
- Wow.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:51.843
That's a lot.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.570
- Maybe the students are mean to them,

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.163
or give 'em a hard time.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.160
- What percent of teachers are affected

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.980
by high stress levels on the job?

00:01:58.980 --> 00:01:59.813
- C?

00:02:00.137 --> 00:02:01.760
- Yes, C, 93%.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.070
- I think it's C, 93%.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:08.843
Because I'm learning that it's
very stressful and expensive.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.011
(bell dinging)
- Yeah.

00:02:10.421 --> 00:02:11.560
- Yeah, that makes sense.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.280
- It makes me realize
how much teachers put in,

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.490
and sometimes they don't
receive it from the students.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.727
- All you hear is like,
"Oh, I hate school.

00:02:17.727 --> 00:02:19.540
"I don't wanna do my
homework, blah blah blah."

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.540
And like, teachers, maybe
some of them it's like

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.240
their dream job to teach,
and to like work in education

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.434
and stuff, so it's kind
of sad that students

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.480
can be rude sometimes.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.090
Like, we should just, you
know, wake up and be happy

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.674
that we're -- you know.

00:02:33.674 --> 00:02:36.237
- Instead of sleeping in
class, and disrespecting. So.

00:02:36.554 --> 00:02:39.137
(gentle music)

